Fix repair barcode label: phone and customer number no longer cut off

Root causes:
1. Label page size was 50mm×25mm but content (store name + barcode + ticket
   number + customer ID/name + phone) totals ~27mm → bottom rows clipped
2. CSS had overflow:hidden + white-space:nowrap on customer-info and phone-info,
   cutting off long names and phone numbers horizontally
3. JSX inline styles also had whiteSpace:'nowrap', overflow:'hidden' which
   overrode print CSS

Fixes applied to all 5 barcode label print locations:
- technician/TicketDetail.tsx
- components/TicketDetailDialog.tsx
- components/ShopTicketDialog.tsx
- technician/NewRepairRequest.tsx
- shop/ShopNewRepair.tsx

Changes:
- @page size increased from 50mm×25mm → 50mm×30mm
- body now uses min-height:30mm, height:auto (not fixed height) so content never overflows
- Removed white-space:nowrap and overflow:hidden from .customer-info/.phone-info
- Added word-break:break-all so long Arabic names wrap instead of being clipped
- Updated margins from 0.2mm → 0.5mm for better vertical spacing
